{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2093","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Simple Repetition"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pasha loves prime numbers$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$! Once again, in his attempts to find a new way to generate prime numbers, he became interested in an algorithm he found on the internet:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" To obtain a new number $$$y$$$, repeat $$$k$$$ times the decimal representation of the number $$$x$$$ (without leading zeros). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, for $$$x = 52$$$ and $$$k = 3$$$, we get $$$y = 525252$$$, and for $$$x = 6$$$ and $$$k = 7$$$, we get $$$y = 6666666$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pasha really wants the resulting number $$$y$$$ to be prime, but he doesn't yet know how to check the primality of numbers generated by this algorithm. Help Pasha and tell him whether $$$y$$$ is prime!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$An integer $$$x$$$ is considered prime if it has "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2$$$ distinct divisors: $$$1$$$ and $$$x$$$. For example, $$$13$$$ is prime because it has only $$$2$$$ divisors: $$$1$$$ and $$$13$$$. Note that the number $$$1$$$ is not prime, as it has only one divisor."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of several sets of input data. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 100$$$) — the number of sets of input data. The following lines describe the sets of input data."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each data set contains two integers: $$$x$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq x \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$1 \\leq k \\leq 7$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each set of input data, output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«YES»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (without quotes) if the resulting number $$$y$$$ will be prime, and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«NO»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«Yes»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«No»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in any case (for example, the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«yES»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«yes»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"«Yes»"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be recognized as positive answers)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n52 3\n6 7\n7 1\n1 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\nNO\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2093C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2093/problem/C"}